        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "LUAS STOP 3 MINUTES WALK/NO RENT CAP\r\n\r\nMarion Earner LWK South Dublin is delighted to present to the market this recently upgraded and extended two bed ground floor Duplex which is presented in show-house condition throughout with stylish interiors and set in a most convenient location.\r\nThe current proud owners have upgraded this property with the addition of a stunning new kitchen, new modern bathroom and quality flooring through out . The result is a most appealing and contempary low maintenance property located within in this mature and most sought-after development.\r\n\r\nUpon entering the property, one is welcomed by a bright hall area with the benefit of a glazed door and window panel which lead into the main living/dining area which has been extended. This open plan space is ideal for entertaining, with a feature open fireplace and an extended dining area over looking the front terrace.The  entire property having been fully refurbished in November 2023.\r\nAccommodation  briefly comprises entrance porch, large extended living/dining room, separate kitchen, 2 large double bedrooms and a family bathroom, front terrace and private driveway. Outside to the front there is a cobble lock drive with off street parking and a neat lawn area.\r\n\r\nThe property is set within the much sought-after and well regarded Druid Valley development.Local amenities here include Tesco,Cafe,Restaurant,Barbers,Creche and playground all within walking distance. There are excellent transport options with the Luas stop at Cherrywood a leisurely three-minute stroll and M50, exit 16 and N11 (QBC) are both easily accessible. There are a variety of local  bus routes including Bus Eireann Routes and the  24 hr Airport Bus.\r\n \r\nDruid Valley is close to a variety of local amenities in nearby Cabinteely Village including many specialist shops, restaurants, coffee houses, bars, a local library, and Cornelscourt Shopping Centre (Dunnes Stores). The development also offers an on-site crèche, The Park Academy, open green spaces, and landscaped grounds. The new Cherrywood town centre is going to bring a big change to the area, there will be a variety of retailers including shops, boutiques, cinema, and other leisure and entertainment outlets as well as restaurants, bars, and a hotel. There are three newly opened parks in Cherrywood in addition to the already existing parks at Cabinteely and Kilbogget which offer various walks, sporting, and recreational amenities. Cherrywood Business Park is located opposite the development which has shops, cafes, and Ben Dunne leisure facility.\r\n\r\nThere are several top rated junior and senior schools in the vicinity, including St Brigid's National Schools, St. Columbanus National School, St. Laurence College, Cabinteely Community School, Rathdown School, St. Joseph of Cluny, to name but a few.\r\n\r\n Early viewing is strongly advised.\r\n\r\n***All information provided is to the best of our knowledge. The utmost of care and attention has been placed on providing factual and correct information. In certain cases some information may have been provided by the vendor to us. We do not hold any responsibility for mistakes, errors or inaccuracies in our online advertising and give each and every viewer the right to get an opinion on any concern they may have***"
      },
